uests":1},"T5c":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":15648.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":680.0,"requests":2},"T5e":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1050.3333333333333,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":86.5,"requests":1},"T6":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1050.3333333333333,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":86.5,"requests":1},"T9":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1050.3333333333333,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":86.5,"requests":1},"necessity":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":2081.75,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":370.5,"requests":1},"project.portability":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1050.3333333333333,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":86.5,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":27243.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":961.0,"requests":2}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify that each project's base-query results are buffered into a per-project staging dict (with its own seen set) and merged into the shared `snapshot`/`seen_keys` ONLY after both that project's queries complete successfully, so a skip discards all of that project's partial pages atomically.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Current loop merges each page directly: `snapshot[key] = {k: fields[k] ...}` (line 583) and adds to `seen_keys` (line 579) as pages arrive from `_iter_pages`","A per-project base fetch is TWO queries (active + done-recent); a failure on the second (or mid-pagination of the first) occurs after some keys are already in the shared snapshot","Plan states the try/except is 'scoped PER PROJECT (both the active and done-recent query for a project share the boundary)' but does not specify buffering/rollback of already-merged keys"],"finding":"The plan's mechanism (wrap each project's base-query fetch in a per-project try/except and continue) does not by itself guarantee its stated 'do not merge partial results that would look like deletions' property, because the current loop merges pages into the shared `snapshot` dict (and populates `seen_keys`) incrementally — a transport failure mid-pagination of jql_active, or after jql_active merged but jql_done_recent fails, leaves that project's partial keys already committed to the snapshot.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1e3f367321a88690","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'SKIP that project (do not merge partial results that would look like deletions)'; fetcher.py `_build_snapshot` lines 561-583","norm_id":"n43ba3ede82dc3266","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["jql_active(P) paginates and merges 3 pages, then the 4th ACLI call 429s — P's first ~300 issues stay in the snapshot but the rest are absent, and the differ may treat the absent remainder as deletions","jql_active(P) succeeds fully; jql_done_recent(P) raises HTTPError — P's active issues remain merged while the project is nominally 'skipped'"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a `_fetch_project(client, proj, pass_id, repo_root, alert_store)` helper (symmetric to `_enrich_project`) that drains both queries into a LOCAL dict and returns it; `_build_snapshot` calls it inside the per-project try/except and merges the returned dict into `snapshot`/`seen_keys` only on success — on any per-project transport error it emits the `fetcher-project-fetch-failed` alert, discards the local dict, and continues (re-raising BackendPaginationStallError as before). State this atomic-merge requirement in the Approach section so the no-partial-merge contract is guaranteed by construction, not just by intent.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Add a behavioral unit asserting the pass still ABORTS (raises) when a project's base query raises BackendPaginationStallError (and/or an invalid-key raise), not merely a structural assertion that _validate_project_key sits outside the try.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","necessity"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'_validate_project_key is still called by jql_active outside the per-project try, and the boundary re-raises BackendPaginationStallError exactly as _enrich_project does'","Testing section only adds a transport-error skip test (BAD raises HTTPError), no test for the fail-closed re-raise path"],"finding":"AC line 4 verifies the preserved fail-CLOSED behavior (invalid key still raises; BackendPaginationStallError still re-raises) via a STRUCTURAL claim ('_validate_project_key is still called by jql_active outside the per-project try' / 'the boundary re-raises exactly as _enrich_project does') rather than a behavioral test asserting the pass actually aborts on these cases. Since this ticket restructures the try/except scope, a regression could leave the stall/invalid-key inside the new per-project boundary and get silently swallowed — the structural grep would not catch it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f442204be58978706","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 4 / Testing section","norm_id":"n0133aa0f39616b48","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit accidentally moves BackendPaginationStallError handling inside the per-project except, swallowing a truncated read as a skippable fault","An absent-key raise gets caught by the new per-project boundary, silently degrading to a skip instead of failing closed"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a companion unit where _FakeClient raises BackendPaginationStallError for a project and assert _build_snapshot propagates it (no skip, no alert), mirroring the enrichment loop's expected re-raise.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"ch